<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-detection-reserve> {
  ex:l5-concentration-dependent-detection a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Concentration-dependent positive-finding probability"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l5-v03-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "At a fixed concentration, independent repeat classifications under stable conditions can be modelled by a binomial count with a common concentration-specific positive-finding probability. A logistic relation between concentration and log odds is one possible model family, not a physical law or evidence of analytical performance. The unit, concentration coding, matrix, preparation and calibration range must be specified; detection probability at fixed concentration is not target-population prevalence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "One concentration, repeated independent decisions"@en ; cd:body "At fixed concentration c, the number of positive decisions in n c independent repeats with the same probability p of c follows a binomial model. Here ten repeats at 2 mg/L use a specified probability of one half."@en ; cd:latex "K_c\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(n_c,p(c))" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-v03a-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-v03a-count, ex:l5-v03a-concentration, ex:l5-v03a-probability, ex:l5-v03a-law ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-v03a-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and fixed-concentration assumptions"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-v03a-count, ex:l5-v03a-concentration, ex:l5-v03a-probability, ex:l5-v03a-law ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-count a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "positive count and repeat count" ; cd:mathNotation "K_c,\\ n_c" ; cd:body "Random positive-finding count and fixed number of repeats at concentration c. Here n c = 10 and possible counts are 0 through 10."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-concentration a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "fixed concentration" ; cd:mathNotation "c" ; cd:body "Specified stable concentration, here 2 mg/L. Subscript c labels that concentration, not a repeat index or an environmental-population proportion."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-probability a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "positive-finding probability" ; cd:mathNotation "p(c)" ; cd:body "Dimensionless probability of a positive decision at fixed c under this procedure and matrix. Here 0.50, a teaching assumption, not fitted performance."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-law a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "binomial law" ; cd:mathNotation "\\sim,\\ \\operatorname{Bin}(\\ ,\\ )" ; cd:body "Tilde means distributed as; Bin names the binomial model with repeat count and probability. Requires independent decisions with common p at this c."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "A possible logistic model, not a physical law"@en ; cd:body "The natural logarithm of positive-finding odds is modelled as an intercept plus a slope times concentration. The chosen illustration has intercept minus four and slope two litres per milligram."@en ; cd:latex "\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{p(c)}{1-p(c)}\\right)=\\beta_0+\\beta_1 c" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-v03b-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-v03b-probability, ex:l5-v03b-log, ex:l5-v03b-parameters, ex:l5-v03b-units ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-v03b-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols, units and model choice"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-v03b-probability, ex:l5-v03b-log, ex:l5-v03b-parameters, ex:l5-v03b-units ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-probability a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "probability and complement" ; cd:mathNotation "p(c),\\ 1-p(c)" ; cd:body "Positive- and negative-finding probabilities at fixed concentration c. Both are dimensionless; this logistic family keeps p strictly between 0 and 1."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-log a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "natural log odds" ; cd:mathNotation "\\log,\\ p(c)/(1-p(c))" ; cd:body "Log is natural logarithm. Divide positive by negative probability for dimensionless odds; log odds are not a concentration or a probability."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-parameters a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "intercept and slope" ; cd:mathNotation "\\beta_0,\\ \\beta_1" ; cd:body "Subscripts 0 and 1 identify intercept and slope, not powers. Chosen intercept is -4; slope is 2 L/mg. These are not fitted to V02 or calibration data."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-units a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "concentration and arithmetic" ; cd:mathNotation "c,\\ =,\\ +,\\ -,\\ /" ; cd:body "c uses mg/L; multiplying by slope 2 L/mg gives a dimensionless term. Add to dimensionless intercept. Equality defines the model; subtraction and division form odds."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level5-detection-reserve> {
  ex:unit-level5-screening-reserve cd:hasFocusConcept ex:l5-concentration-dependent-detection .
  ex:l5-v03a-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Characterize detection, not the water body"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "An analytical component: detection response"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "State where the analytical model applies"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03a-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Exact binomial probabilities: ten repeats at 2 mg/L"@en ; cd:body "Specified positive probability 0.50 at 2 mg/L. Ten independent repeats. These are model probabilities, not observed frequencies."@en ; cd:chartType cd:BarChart ; cd:chartPresentation "complete" ; cd:usesDataset ex:l5-v03-pmf ; cd:xAxisLabel "Positive decisions in ten repeats"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Probability"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "1" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03b-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Illustrative logistic positive-finding probability"@en ; cd:body "Chosen intercept -4; slope 2 L/mg. Probability 0.50 at 2 mg/L is a model midpoint, not a validated detection limit."@en ; cd:chartType cd:LineChart ; cd:chartPresentation "complete" ; cd:showChartPoints false ; cd:chartYMinimum 0.0 ; cd:chartYMaximum 1.0 ; cd:usesDataset ex:l5-v03-logistic ; cd:xAxisLabel "Fixed concentration"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "mg/L" ; cd:yAxisLabel "Positive-finding probability"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "1" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-v03c-unit, ex:l5-v03c-matrix, ex:l5-v03c-calibration, ex:l5-v03c-model ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-unit a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Define the independent unit"@en ; cd:body "Repeated signals, independently prepared aliquots and separate environmental samples are not interchangeable. Shared drift can correlate decisions."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-matrix a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Hold conditions explicit"@en ; cd:body "State the analyte, decision rule, concentration scale, matrix and preparation. A curve for one set of conditions need not transfer to another."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-calibration a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Calibration needs evidence"@en ; cd:body "Use justified reference concentrations and repeats across the range. Estimated parameters and predicted probabilities carry uncertainty."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03c-model a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "A family, not a natural law"@en ; cd:body "Check fit and range. Neither a drawn sigmoid nor a 50% midpoint establishes a detection limit, accuracy or population prevalence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03-protocol a cd:WorkedExample ; cd:body "A separate specified teaching model, not a calibration of V02's sensitivity or false-positive rate. Concentration c is nonnegative and uses mg/L. The chosen dimensionless log-odds intercept is -4 and slope is 2 L/mg. Positive-finding probability is 1/(1+exp(4-2*c)) when c is expressed numerically in mg/L. The illustrative display covers 0 to 4 mg/L; it is not an experimentally validated calibration range. At c=0 the model gives about 0.017986, at c=1 about 0.119203, at c=2 exactly 0.5, at c=3 about 0.880797 and at c=4 about 0.982014. The nonzero zero-concentration probability is an illustrative baseline finding rate; no real false-positive performance is inferred. At 2 mg/L, ten independent decisions with common probability 0.5 give exact binomial count masses choose(10,k)/1024 for k=0 through 10, mean count 5 and variance 2.5. An expected count of 5 is not a fixed allocation in every realized run. No observations, simulation or parameter fit are claimed. Logistic drawing coordinates are rounded to twelve decimal places and joined linearly; no raw-observation markers are shown. The natural logarithm acts on dimensionless odds. Changing concentration units or centering/coding requires a matching parameter transformation; slope cannot retain its numerical value under arbitrary recoding. A fitted curve requires independent evidence, uncertainty assessment, matrix/preparation scope and a justified observation model. Correlated repeats, changing concentration, varying preparation or drift can violate the simple binomial assumptions. The 50% probability midpoint is not automatically an analytical detection limit or a legal decision threshold. No method validation or environmental prevalence claim is made."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03-pmf a cd:Dataset ; skos:prefLabel "Theoretical binomial count probabilities at concentration 2 mg/L"@en ; cd:derivedFromResource ex:l5-v03-protocol ; cd:hasObservation ex:l5-v03-k0, ex:l5-v03-k1, ex:l5-v03-k2, ex:l5-v03-k3, ex:l5-v03-k4, ex:l5-v03-k5, ex:l5-v03-k6, ex:l5-v03-k7, ex:l5-v03-k8, ex:l5-v03-k9, ex:l5-v03-k10 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03-k0 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "0"@en ; cd:numericValue 0.0009765625 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-v03-k1 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "1"@en ; cd:numericValue 0.009765625 ; cd:authoredResource true .
